    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: City Commuters Rainy-Day Planning</h1>
    <p>A tourist can cancel a ride when the sky turns; a commuter cannot, because the office opens at eight whether it is raining or not. That single fact changes rainy-day riding from an occasional hazard into a planned part of the commute, and it is the reason this chapter exists. Rainy-day planning for a city commuter is about three things in order: staying visible, keeping traction honest, and building a set of habits and gear choices that make the wet commute as routine as the dry one. None of it is complicated, and all of it is worth setting up in the first week of the rental, before the season tests it.</p>
    <p>This page is the rain chapter of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster for city commuters. Rental prices for the daily, weekly and monthly tiers are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, general questions live on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the two chapters closest to this one are the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/city-commuters-traffic-preparation/">traffic preparation guide</a> and the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/city-commuters-pre-ride-inspection/">pre-ride inspection routine</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
